# ---- Counted nouns ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Finnish plural rule (assets/i18n): one (1) | other (0, 2, 3 ... 21 ...). After any number but 1 the
# noun is in the partitive singular: "yksi siirto", "kolme siirtoa", "kaksikymmentäyksi siirtoa".
# The default keys are the subject / complement forms ("Vain {n:mistake} koko pelissä.").
# Other cases (both the number and its noun take the case; the noun stays singular):
#   _acc   object of an active verb: "Teit {n:mistake_acc}." = "yhden virheen" / "kolme virhettä"
#          (written "1 virheen" / "3 virhettä"). After an imperative or a passive: the default.
#   _gen   "{n:move_gen} ajan" = "kolmen siirron ajan", "{n:point_gen} etu", "{n:square_gen} päässä"
#   _part  "{n:piece_part} vastaan" = "kahta nappulaa vastaan"
#   _ine   "matti {m:move_ine}" = "matti kolmessa siirrossa" (mate in three)
#   _ela   "{n:move_ela}" = "kolmesta siirrosta" (out of / from three moves)
#   _ill   "{n:point_ill} asti" = "kolmeen pisteeseen asti"
#   _ade   "{n:point_ade} tappiolla" = "kolmella pisteellä tappiolla", "{n:piece_ade}" (with three pieces)
# Every noun has them except "time" (kerta): "kerran" / "kolme kertaa" only.
# A number alone in a case: "{n:acc}" (yhden / kolme), "{n:gen}", "{n:part}", "{n:ine}", "{n:ela}",
# "{n:ill}", "{n:ade}" (count.<case> at the end of this section).
